WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.060
Speaker 1: Well, my friends, inflation is down&nbsp;
significantly and Joe Biden's approval rating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:12.600
continues to climb in a horrible turn of events&nbsp;
for the right, which wants to continue to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:18.720
the lie that Democratic presidents are terrible&nbsp;
for the economy. Now, you all know that I don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.640
actually play these games when it comes to the&nbsp;
economy. You all know that when we talk like this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:28.800
it's sort of tongue in cheek, because the reality&nbsp;
is that on many of these issues, presidents have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.820
very little influence one way or the other.&nbsp;
I don't play the gas prices game. I will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:38.280
jokingly say, how did Joe Biden get gas prices&nbsp;
to be down a dollar 70 per gallon as they are?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.840
But of course, I don't really give him credit&nbsp;
for that. The same way that I don't blame him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.760
for the fact that gas prices went up. But for&nbsp;
the right wingers that see the world in this way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:54.540
we should be aware of what is going on. And&nbsp;
as I'm an idiot when it comes to this stuff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.540 --> 00:01:01.980
but I predicted we would get down into the sixes&nbsp;
in the first part of 2023 and inflation would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:07.920
probably be down into the four or fives by the&nbsp;
middle or third quarter of 2023. And we continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.360
to go in that direction. We learned this morning&nbsp;
CNBC report consumer prices fell 0.1% in December&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:24.060
in line with expectations. Excluding food and&nbsp;
energy, core CPI rose 0.3% on an annual basis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:34.380
Headline CPI, meaning top line inflation, is now&nbsp;
up 6.5%, while core inflation is up 5.7%. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:39.600
biggest reason for the easing in inflation&nbsp;
came from a sharp drop in gasoline prices,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:45.420
which are now lower on a year over year basis.&nbsp;
I want to tell everybody again, because people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:51.540
are so confused and they write to me things&nbsp;
that make no sense. When we talk about 6.5%,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:59.580
what we're talking about is over the last year. So&nbsp;
we just got the December numbers. So when we now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:07.860
say year over year, we're talking about price&nbsp;
increase from December 2021 to December 2022.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:15.900
Every month you shift by one month. What is the 12&nbsp;
month period we're talking about? So in December,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:24.420
when we got the November number, we were talking&nbsp;
about inflation from November 21 to November 22.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:32.820
It's now January. We've now added the December&nbsp;
22 inflation data and removed the November 21.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:38.640
So we've changed the range Instead of November 21&nbsp;
to November 22. We're now talking about December&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:45.660
21 to December 22. That inflation number is down&nbsp;
from being in the eights to 6.5%. That is what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:52.020
we are talking about when we talk about inflation.&nbsp;
This is now six months in a row that inflation has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:59.940
come down. Core inflation from October to December&nbsp;
was only 3.1% annualized. That's the lowest such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:07.440
reading in 15 months. Gas, as I mentioned,&nbsp;
is down a dollar 70 per gallon from its peak.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:12.720
Food inflation is slowing. Last month we saw&nbsp;
actually the smallest increase in food prices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:19.800
in almost two years. The cost of goods is falling&nbsp;
for electronics. Used car prices have come down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:25.560
which got completely out of control. Wages are&nbsp;
higher now than six months ago, so it's not.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:30.060
Prices are coming down and so are wages. Wages&nbsp;
are still higher, prices are lower when you adjust&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:37.500
everything for inflation. We have the lowest&nbsp;
unemployment rate in 50 years and it is at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:45.900
partially being perceived by voters as Joe Biden&nbsp;
being a generally good steward of the economy. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:51.480
don't have to believe, as I don't believe, that&nbsp;
every one of these numbers is related to who's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:56.040
president. I didn't believe it under Trump, and I&nbsp;
don't believe it's the case under Biden. I'm not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:02.520
playing games with that. But when you see the&nbsp;
zoomed out version of what's happening in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:08.880
country, you see a pretty steady uptrend in Joe&nbsp;
Biden's approval, which bottomed out in late July.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:14.700
And as you if you're looking on the screen,&nbsp;
it's been up, up, up. And there's a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:20.520
little uptick here even in the last week where&nbsp;
Joe Biden's approval is now up to 44%. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:27.780
you might say 44%. That's terrible. Yeah. I&nbsp;
mean, listen, the point here is. In the modern,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:36.240
hyper polarized climate of American politics. You&nbsp;
look at Bush, Obama and Trump approvals over time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:44.820
44% at this point in one's term is actually just&nbsp;
fine. It's uncontroversial is the point. The idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:50.280
that the country is furious and disgusted with&nbsp;
Joe Biden, it's just not borne out in the data.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:56.640
So skip the David, you're a Democratic shill&nbsp;
stuff. I've never been a registered Democrat. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:00.300
don't care about Joe Biden. I don't care about&nbsp;
the Democratic Party. What I'm coming to you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:06.540
and saying is the American people are realizing&nbsp;
that what Republicans are offering is nonsense.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:12.420
If you look at the Republican priorities that&nbsp;
have been made clear since they took over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:18.600
House of Representatives very recently, their&nbsp;
ideas benefit the super wealthy. They want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:26.700
essentially help the wealthy avoid taxes at the&nbsp;
expense of ordinary middle class taxpayers. House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:32.100
Republicans introduced a bill to block actions&nbsp;
that would lower gas prices. They gutted a bunch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:39.060
of ethics requirements. They are pushing a bill&nbsp;
that would actually increase tax rates on middle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:45.960
class families at the net effective level.&nbsp;
And they're open to open to cuts to Social&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:49.560
Security and Medicare. That's what Republicans&nbsp;
are offering now. Hopefully, they won't get any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:54.960
of it done because the Republicans don't control&nbsp;
the Senate. But inflation numbers improving. Very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.960 --> 00:06:00.660
good economic numbers. You see what Republicans&nbsp;
are offering. It makes sense that Joe Biden's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:06.840
approval keeps ticking up. And quite frankly,&nbsp;
18 months ago, yeah, 12 months ago, roughly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:12.060
I would not have said Joe Biden is&nbsp;
well-positioned for reelection in 2024.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:16.080
Right now, I think Joe Biden is dramatically&nbsp;
better positioned for reelection. Doesn't mean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:21.120
he is running or should run or shouldn't run,&nbsp;
but just based on the data, the economy is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:27.120
quite strong and that tends to bode well when&nbsp;
presidents argue for their own reelection.

